[{"text":"2 Read the text again. Complete gaps 1-5 with","y":0.046337157885313784,"h":0.0132558650919955,"x":0.094650218289619018,"w":0.35802467346191408},{"text":"sentences A-F. There is one extra sentence.","h":0.01191526919682262,"x":0.11728395786131546,"y":0.060900264940359938,"w":0.31893003463745112},{"y":0.081200352940163589,"x":0.11934157025023406,"text":"A Instead, he communicated with them by ringing","w":0.35185184478759768,"h":0.013276390974645724},{"w":0.28189300537109374,"x":0.1399176983689798,"text":"a bell and leaving notes in special boxes.","y":0.095763459951605068,"h":0.011915269196822509},{"y":0.11032656655111028,"w":0.34567901611328122,"x":0.11728394304075326,"text":"B He had another beautiful house in London and","h":0.01191526919682262},{"y":0.12645348844060544,"w":0.1707818794250488,"x":0.13991770510914897,"text":"sometimes stayed there.","h":0.01167537296965182},{"h":0.01191526919682262,"w":0.32510288238525398,"x":0.11728395381766102,"y":0.14077669893406397,"text":"C A third unusual thing about him was that he"},{"y":0.15533980572736772,"text":"hated all kinds of dancing.","w":0.18106994628906251,"x":0.13991770401596257,"h":0.01191526919682262},{"y":0.16990291259621593,"x":0.11728395671652947,"text":"D For example, he gave each servant an umbrella","w":0.34979423522949221,"h":0.013239187996469504},{"x":0.13786008093651045,"w":0.32921810150146491,"h":0.013239187996469504,"text":"and bought horses for them to ride through the","y":0.1844660194621941},{"text":"gardens and in the tunnels under his house.","x":0.13786009397380805,"y":0.19902912641912973,"w":0.30246912002563481,"h":0.011915269196822509},{"h":0.013239187996469615,"w":0.37037036895751951,"x":0.1152263418586887,"y":0.21359223290708629,"text":"E He often wore two or more coats at the same time"},{"w":0.3436214065551757,"h":0.01191526919682262,"text":"and a very strange hat - it was nearly a metre tall.","x":0.13786008291068361,"y":0.22947925864462215},{"y":0.24404236552437153,"w":0.37242797851562498,"text":"F For instance, he built an underground ballroom with","x":0.11522634368457424,"h":0.013239187996469504},{"text":"space for 2,000 guests, but he never used it because","x":0.1358024843901959,"w":0.36008228302001954,"y":0.25860547227043695,"h":0.013239187996469504},{"w":0.21399175643920898,"text":"he was too shy to invite anyone.","h":0.01191526919682262,"x":0.13580247925638994,"y":0.27316857891552171},{"text":"3 Read the questions and underline the parts of the","x":0.090335554629195555,"w":0.38513568878173821,"y":0.29208472562804566,"h":0.015489718815129283},{"text":"text with the answers.","y":0.30803177396310399,"w":0.16460905075073243,"h":0.01191526919682262,"x":0.11111111454232922},{"h":0.013640243819826869,"y":0.32384841530890585,"text":"1 What was unusual about the Duke's hat?","w":0.30275741577148435,"x":0.11301468952989346},{"w":0.29629629135131841,"h":0.011627906839719149,"x":0.11111111126878534,"text":"2 Why did he write notes to his servants?","y":0.34156976765572189},{"x":0.11111111051869343,"w":0.28600822448730467,"y":0.35610465130397762,"h":0.01162790683971926,"text":"3 How did his servants deliver his food?"},{"x":0.11111112970545033,"y":0.37202118261833239,"w":0.36213989257812501,"text":"4 Why was the underground ballroom never used?","h":0.013239187996469615},{"h":0.013254582303241613,"x":0.11111112970545033,"y":0.38790820813530802,"w":0.36213989257812501,"text":"5 How did the Duke's grandfather get the house in"},{"x":0.13368267911753659,"h":0.010570053073650776,"y":0.40241846189472175,"text":"London?","w":0.063910360336303706},{"h":0.013081394879037367,"text":"6 How long was the roof of the riding school?","w":0.32510288238525387,"y":0.41860465156120807,"x":0.11111111287115896},{"x":0.11111111330210739,"text":"7 What was in the room with the toilet?","y":0.4345930230852646,"w":0.2818930053710938,"h":0.010243693601737824},{"text":"VOCABULARY PRACTICE | Landscape features","x":0.086302609291052115,"y":0.45635447931751827,"h":